{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy makes random_walk the default in clear space, inserts a short move_forward pulse after a clear random walk to bias coverage, and routes every obstacle event through dedicated recovery states with exactly one safe action. Action/commit states self-loop on path_clear so intended pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification for exploration/recovery flow and one alternation specification to avoid long forward streaks by requiring random_walk before move_forward."
  ],
